"explanation": "In an electrical circuit, a switch is the component specifically designed to open or close the circuit. When a switch is opened, it breaks the conductive path, thereby stopping the flow of electric current. Wires conduct current, batteries provide the voltage/energy source, and bulbs consume energy as loads, but none of these are primarily used to stop current flow in the manner a switch is.",
